    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:format dcterms:MediaType)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:instructionalMethod dcterms:MethodOfInstruction)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:language dcterms:LinguisticSystem)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:license dcterms:LicenseDocument)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:mediator dcterms:AgentClass)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:medium dcterms:PhysicalMedium)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:provenance dcterms:ProvenanceStatement)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:publisher dcterms:Agent)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:rights dcterms:RightsStatement)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:rightsHolder dcterms:Agent)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:spatial dcterms:Location)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcam:rangeIncludes dcterms:temporal dcterms:PeriodOfTime)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:LinguisticSystem "Written, spoken, sign, and computer languages are linguistic systems."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:PhysicalMedium "Examples include paper, canvas, or DVD."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:RFC3066 "RFC 3066 has been obsoleted by RFC 4646."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:RFC4646 "RFC 4646 obsoletes RFC 3066."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:RFC5646 "RFC 5646 obsoletes RFC 4646."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:SizeOrDuration "Examples include a number of pages, a specification of length, width, and breadth, or a period in hours, minutes, and seconds."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:accessRights "Access Rights may include information regarding access or restrictions based on privacy, security, or other policies."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:accrualMethod "Recommended practice is to use a value from the Collection Description Accrual Method Vocabulary [[DCMI-ACCRUALMETHOD](https://dublincore.org/groups/collections/accrual-method/)]."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:accrualPeriodicity "Recommended practice is to use a value from the Collection Description Frequency Vocabulary [[DCMI-COLLFREQ](https://dublincore.org/groups/collections/frequency/)]."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:accrualPolicy "Recommended practice is to use a value from the Collection Description Accrual Policy Vocabulary [[DCMI-ACCRUALPOLICY](https://dublincore.org/groups/collections/accrual-policy/)]."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:alternative "The distinction between titles and alternative titles is application-specific."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:audience "Recommended practice is to use this property with non-literal values from a vocabulary of audience types."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:available "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Recommended practice is to include sufficient bibliographic detail to identify the resource as unambiguously as possible."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:contributor "The guidelines for using names of persons or organizations as creators apply to contributors."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:coverage "Spatial topic and spatial applicability may be a named place or a location specified by its geographic coordinates. Temporal topic may be a named period, date, or date range. A jurisdiction may be a named administrative entity or a geographic place to which the resource applies. Recommended practice is to use a controlled vocabulary such as the Getty Thesaurus of Geographic Names [[TGN](https://www.getty.edu/research/tools/vocabulary/tgn/index.html)]. Where appropriate, named places or time periods may be used in preference to numeric identifiers such as sets of coordinates or date ranges.  Because coverage is so broadly defined, it is preferable to use the more specific subproperties Temporal Coverage and Spatial Coverage."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:created "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:creator "Recommended practice is to identify the creator with a URI.  If this is not possible or feasible, a literal value that identifies the creator may be provided."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:date "Date may be used to express temporal information at any level of granularity.  Recommended practice is to express the date, date/time, or period of time according to ISO 8601-1 [[ISO 8601-1](https://www.iso.org/iso-8601-date-and-time-format.html)] or a published profile of the ISO standard, such as the W3C Note on Date and Time Formats [[W3CDTF](https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-datetime)] or the Extended Date/Time Format Specification [[EDTF](http://www.loc.gov/standards/datetime/)].  If the full date is unknown, month and year (YYYY-MM) or just year (YYYY) may be used. Date ranges may be specified using ISO 8601 period of time specification in which start and end dates are separated by a '/' (slash) character.  Either the start or end date may be missing."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:dateAccepted "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty.  Examples of resources to which a date of acceptance may be relevant are a thesis (accepted by a university department) or an article (accepted by a journal)."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:dateCopyrighted "Typically a year.  Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:dateSubmitted "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty.  Examples of resources to which a 'Date Submitted' may be relevant include a thesis (submitted to a university department) or an article (submitted to a journal)."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:description "Description may include but is not limited to: an abstract, a table of contents, a graphical representation, or a free-text account of the resource."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:extent "Recommended practice is to specify the file size in megabytes and duration in ISO 8601 format."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:format "Recommended practice is to use a controlled vocabulary where available. For example, for file formats one could use the list of Internet Media Types [[MIME](https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml)].  Examples of dimensions include size and duration."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:hasFormat "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Format Of."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:hasPart "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Part Of."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:hasVersion "Changes in version imply substantive changes in content rather than differences in format. This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Version Of."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:identifier "Recommended practice is to identify the resource by means of a string conforming to an identification system. Examples include International Standard Book Number (ISBN), Digital Object Identifier (DOI), and Uniform Resource Name (URN).  Persistent identifiers should be provided as HTTP URIs."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:instructionalMethod "Instructional Method typically includes ways of presenting instructional materials or conducting instructional activities, patterns of learner-to-learner and learner-to-instructor interactions, and mechanisms by which group and individual levels of learning are measured.  Instructional methods include all aspects of the instruction and learning processes from planning and implementation through evaluation and feedback."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isFormatOf "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Has Format."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isPartOf "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Has Part."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isReferencedBy "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of References."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isReplacedBy "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Replaces."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isRequiredBy "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Requires."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:isVersionOf "Changes in version imply substantive changes in content rather than differences in format. This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Has Version."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:issued "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:language "Recommended practice is to use either a non-literal value representing a language from a controlled vocabulary such as ISO 639-2 or ISO 639-3, or a literal value consisting of an IETF Best Current Practice 47 [[IETF-BCP47](https://tools.ietf.org/html/bcp47)] language tag."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:license "Recommended practice is to identify the license document with a URI. If this is not possible or feasible, a literal value that identifies the license may be provided."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:mediator "In an educational context, a mediator might be a parent, teacher, teaching assistant, or care-giver."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:modified "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:provenance "The statement may include a description of any changes successive custodians made to the resource."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:references "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Referenced By."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:relation "Recommended practice is to identify the related resource by means of a URI.  If this is not possible or feasible, a string conforming to a formal identification system may be provided."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:replaces "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Replaced By."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:requires "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of Is Required By."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:rights "Typically, rights information includes a statement about various property rights associated with the resource, including intellectual property rights.  Recommended practice is to refer to a rights statement with a URI.  If this is not possible or feasible, a literal value (name, label, or short text) may be provided."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:rightsHolder "Recommended practice is to refer to the rights holder with a URI. If this is not possible or feasible, a literal value that identifies the rights holder may be provided."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:source "This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. The described resource may be derived from the related resource in whole or in part. Best practice is to identify the related resource by means of a URI or a string conforming to a formal identification system."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:subject "Recommended practice is to refer to the subject with a URI. If this is not possible or feasible, a literal value that identifies the subject may be provided. Both should preferably refer to a subject in a controlled vocabulary."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:type "Recommended practice is to use a controlled vocabulary such as the DCMI Type Vocabulary [[DCMI-TYPE](http://dublincore.org/documents/dcmi-type-vocabulary/)]. To describe the file format, physical medium, or dimensions of the resource, use the property Format."@en)
    AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description dcterms:valid "Recommended practice is to describe the date, date/time, or period of time as recommended for the property Date, of which this is a subproperty."@en)
